# wheel-burst (M9): three wheel notches in one frame over the plane (CartesianPlane.test.tsx: "zooms
# one notch per wheel event, however many land before a render"). The pointer at (1106, 338) is
# (618, 246) in the plane, 150 px right of its centre and 150 above, as the test's (450, 150) on its
# 600 x 600 plane; each notch of −100 px scales the zoom by exp(0.15) about the pointer, from where
# the last left the view: 50 · exp(0.45) = 78.42 px a unit, the maths under the pointer kept
# there. Chromium hands Playwright's wheel over at half its delta under a device scale of 2, on the
# reference too: 50 · exp(0.225) there.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
move 1106 338
wait 500
shot before
wheel 0 -100
wheel 0 -100
wheel 0 -100
wait 16
shot burst
